# merge=union applies only to LOCAL merges -- GitHub's server-side PR merge
# ignores merge drivers. That is fine: the nightly sweep's conflict self-heal
# (tools/repo-sweep.py) runs `git merge origin/main` locally on the sweep
# branch, where these rules take effect, then pushes the healed result.
#
# Scope deliberately narrow: append-only ledger tables ONLY. Never add code,
# YAML/JSON, or narrative prose here -- union silently interleaves text.
# Session files carry YAML frontmatter counters that union can duplicate;
# `repo-sweep.py --normalize-sessions` recomputes them from the body.
docs/friction-register.md merge=union
docs/anneal-ledger.md merge=union
docs/INDEX.md merge=union
docs/sessions/*.md merge=union
